{"name":"Noble Robe","hex":"#807070","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"noble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An aristocrat; one of aristocratic blood. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A medieval gold coin of England in the 14th and 15th centuries, usually valued at 6s 8d."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having honorable qualities; having moral eminence and freedom from anything petty, mean or dubious in conduct and character.","Grand; stately; magnificent; splendid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noble"},{"term":"robe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long loose outer garment, often signifying honorary stature.","The skin of an animal, especially the bison, dressed with the fur on, and used as a wrap."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clothe; to dress.","To put on official vestments."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Robe","blocks":[{"text":"A robe is a loose-fitting outer garment. Unlike garments described as capes or cloaks, robes usually have sleeves. The English word robe derives from Middle English robe (\"garment\"), borrowed from Old French robe, itself taken from the Frankish word *rouba, and is related to the word rob."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/LongPao.JPG/330px-LongPao.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robe","wikidata":"Q345127"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Daggeru.jpg/500px-Daggeru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Daggeru.jpg/500px-Daggeru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Academic robes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaggeru.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi